  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In a January 2025 statement, Travis Hill said the FDIC should consider issuing additional guidance on topics including artificial intelligence, fintech partnerships, and digital assets and tokenization. In a June 2024 statement, he cited artificial intelligence and blockchain as examples of technology that could increase the effectiveness and efficiency of transaction monitoring. In March 2026, he said AI and other new technologies can improve the BSA regime by identifying suspicious activity and reducing false positives, and that the FDIC wants banks to innovate in this space with a supervisory approach that encourages it. In June 2026, he said a proposal encourages responsible innovation and the use of emerging technologies such as artificial intelligence to detect and disrupt illicit finance activity more effectively.",
   "sids": [
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s5",
    "s4"
   ],
